sequenceDiagram
    participant CI as CI/CD Pipeline
    participant TR as Test Runner (Go)<br/>test-runner-image
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS1.2+
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS1.2+
    participant KFTO as Kubeflow Training Op v1
    participant TV2 as Kubeflow Trainer v2
    participant Launcher as Launcher Pod<br/>(mpirun)
    participant Workers as Worker Pods<br/>(orted)
    participant GPU as GPU Hardware<br/>CUDA / ROCm
    participant Prom as Prometheus<br/>9090/TCP HTTPS
    participant WBC as OpenShift Workbench<br/>Controller
    participant Jupyter as Universal Image<br/>8888/TCP HTTP

    rect rgb(220, 240, 255)
        Note over CI,Prom: Flow 1: Integration Test Execution
        CI->>TR: Launch test binary
        TR->>K8s: Create namespace, RBAC<br/>Auth: kubeconfig Bearer Token
        TR->>S3: Upload training data<br/>Auth: AWS credentials
        TR->>K8s: Create PyTorchJob / TrainJob CR
        K8s-->>KFTO: Watch: PyTorchJob created
        K8s-->>TV2: Watch: TrainJob created
        KFTO->>K8s: Create training Pods
        TV2->>K8s: Create JobSet → training Pods
        Note over TR,K8s: Test polls for Pod completion
        TR->>Prom: Query GPU utilization<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
        Prom-->>TR: PromQL metrics
        TR->>K8s: Assert CRD status, cleanup
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 220)
        Note over Launcher,GPU: Flow 2: MPI Distributed Training
        KFTO->>Launcher: Start launcher pod (mpirun)
        Launcher->>Workers: SSH connect<br/>Port: 2222/TCP<br/>Auth: Pre-shared SSH keys
        Workers->>Workers: NCCL/RCCL all-reduce<br/>RDMA/InfiniBand
        Workers->>GPU: Compute forward/backward pass<br/>PCIe/NVLink
        GPU-->>Workers: Gradient results
        Workers-->>Launcher: Training complete
    end

    rect rgb(220, 255, 220)
        Note over WBC,Jupyter: Flow 3: Universal Image Dual-Mode
        alt Workbench Mode (NOTEBOOK_ARGS set)
            WBC->>Jupyter: Inject NOTEBOOK_ARGS env
            Jupyter->>Jupyter: Start Jupyter server<br/>Port: 8888/TCP
        else Training Mode (entrypoint override)
            TV2->>Jupyter: Override entrypoint<br/>Run training command
            Jupyter->>GPU: Execute training
        end
    end
